WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.470
- I'm a Pisces.

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:02.400
- Oh is it, when's your birthday?

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.240
- 23rd of February--
- Me being like, exposing

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:05.073
myself as somebody who's like,

00:00:05.073 --> 00:00:06.594
"Oh, I love horoscopes, I'm a Scorpio."

00:00:06.594 --> 00:00:08.553
- Are you, oh so you're a water sign?

00:00:08.553 --> 00:00:09.750
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:10.980
We're supposed to get on.
- Yeah.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:11.970
- Okay.
- For sure.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.266
I get that though.
- Yeah, yippy!

00:00:14.266 --> 00:00:15.770
(Gena and Little laugh)

00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:18.777
- Hi I'm Gena, I'm here with
musician and actor Little Simz,

00:00:18.777 --> 00:00:22.503
who plays Shelly in Top Boy,
and these are her Netflix IX.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:27.218
What is is like starring in a show that is

00:00:27.218 --> 00:00:29.320
so big, so important to the culture,

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.070
something that I assume
you may have watched

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:31.968
when you were like in school or whatever?

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:33.256
- Yeah.
- What's it Like?

00:00:33.256 --> 00:00:34.089
- Sureal.

00:00:35.064 --> 00:00:37.094
This is something I use to
want when I was younger.

00:00:37.094 --> 00:00:39.960
And just remember feeling like,

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.610
finally, there's something on television

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:44.236
that represented us our our story,

00:00:44.236 --> 00:00:46.200
and you know, our culture.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.011
And add six years on to be a part of that.

00:00:49.011 --> 00:00:51.310
Blessed to be a part of it, for sure.

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:53.065
- What was your reaction
when you got the call

00:00:53.065 --> 00:00:55.083
about like, okay, come
be in Top Boy (mumbles)?

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:58.490
- Um, biggest smile on my face.

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:01.750
And like I'm a smiler,
but when I got this news

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:04.060
it's like, my cheeks were high,

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:07.020
and I just couldn't contain my excitement.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.742
Straight away, called my mom.
- Yeah.

00:01:08.742 --> 00:01:11.510
Tell my sisters, tell my brother,

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:13.540
and just everyone was super-happy.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.640
- In Top Boy, you play Shelly.
- Mm hm.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.895
- What drew you to the role,
and without any spoilers,

00:01:17.895 --> 00:01:19.960
what can the audiences look forward to

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:21.020
in terms of that character?

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:23.190
- Her independence, her ambition,

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:25.430
her fight, and wanting to do more,

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:28.011
be better regardless of you know,

00:01:28.011 --> 00:01:30.320
the environment she came from,

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.120
the circumstances she
circumstances she grew up in.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.620
- Yeah.
- The last seasons,

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:39.000
you didn't really see
like a female perspective.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.870
It was always like, very
from the guy's perspective.

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:44.220
And I think these boys, they have moms,

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:46.700
they've got sisters,
they've got girlfriends.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:50.561
Their decisions and what they
choose to do affects also.

00:01:50.561 --> 00:01:53.820
So I think what's great
about this new season

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:57.715
is you get to see it from
that female perspective.

00:01:57.715 --> 00:01:59.970
- So when it comes to your acting,

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.842
did you always know that
you wanted to do acting?

00:02:01.842 --> 00:02:03.650
Did that come hand-in-hand with

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:05.240
you realizing that you wanted to do music?

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:06.465
- Yeah, for sure, it's...

00:02:06.465 --> 00:02:10.386
I started acting like before
I even got into music.

00:02:10.386 --> 00:02:12.230
- Okay.
Anything within the performing

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.420
arts I just naturally gravitated towards.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:17.040
So parts and things, it didn't feel alien.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:17.970
It didn't feel foreign.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:21.189
It felt like making that
switch between the two

00:02:21.189 --> 00:02:23.680
didn't feel like a challenge to me.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:26.790
Sometimes musicians or artist,

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.060
like when they get a role for something,

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:32.010
they bring their whole
artistry to, like the role.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:33.550
- Yeah.
- And I think it's important

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:36.959
to separate the two.

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:40.386
- Get you a girl that can do
both, 'cause you can (mumbles).

00:02:40.386 --> 00:02:41.219
(Little laughs)
- Okay let's talk

00:02:41.219 --> 00:02:43.620
about inspiration: Who's
your biggest inspiration,

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:46.069
or one of your biggest inspirations
that comes to creating?

00:02:46.069 --> 00:02:47.810
- For sure, it would be Lauryn Hill.

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.535
- Ooh, that's a really good choice.

00:02:49.535 --> 00:02:53.020
- Mm hm, killed it with acting and is a

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.780
very rare talented artist, writer,

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:59.060
and she just does it well,
you know what I'm saying?

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:01.080
I know what it feels like,
when you see her in Sister Act,

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.410
of course, that's Lauryn Hill.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:05.290
But there's also a very
talented actor, a star--

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.250
- Absolutely, I almost
like, sometimes don't

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.460
even connect the two,
because she's so...yeah.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:11.120
- Right, right, but I think that's great.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.641
And it's like, it's been a very big

00:03:12.641 --> 00:03:14.450
inspiration for me for sure.

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:15.980
- All right, if I were to describe you,

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:19.060
I'd say your demeanor is
very cool, calm, collected.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:20.858
Opposite of mine, which is less chill.

00:03:20.858 --> 00:03:23.682
Um, but if you were to sum
yourself up in three words,

00:03:23.682 --> 00:03:25.620
what would those three words be?

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:26.599
How would you describe yourself?

00:03:26.599 --> 00:03:31.599
- A thinker, compassionate, and ambitious.

00:03:31.722 --> 00:03:33.630
- So let's go back to music a little bit.

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:35.110
Check that I've done my homework properly.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:37.100
One of your first gigs was
at the O2 in Islington?

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.630
- Yeah.
- Right.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:41.000
- What's been your
favorite gig of all time,

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.630
if that was kind of like the
foundation of it started--

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:44.940
- All time...
- Yeah.

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:46.850
- I done a lot of shows, you know?

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:48.193
- Yeah, because you're famous, but...

00:03:48.193 --> 00:03:49.635
(Gena and Little laugh loudly)

00:03:49.635 --> 00:03:52.660
- Em, that show, the
show you just mentioned,

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:54.870
The O2 Academy, because I was so young.

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:56.180
And I think getting on that stage,

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:58.384
and it all clicking, like yeah!

00:03:58.384 --> 00:04:00.030
I'm meant to be doing this.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:03.770
Fast forward, years later,
um Glastonbury this year.

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:07.300
- Ooh! Oh my gosh, I can't even imagine.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.133
Woo!

00:04:08.133 --> 00:04:11.480
Three people, dead or alive,

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:15.089
to go to dinner with; who
would they be, and why?

00:04:15.089 --> 00:04:18.303
- Michelle Obama, Oprah,

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:21.890
and Bionce.
(Gena blows loudly)

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:24.002
- I'd just be serving.
(Little laughs)

00:04:24.002 --> 00:04:25.021
And water? (mumbles)

00:04:25.021 --> 00:04:26.417
(Gena laughs loudly)

00:04:26.417 --> 00:04:28.729
- They're just really strong

00:04:28.729 --> 00:04:29.562
powerful black women that I just

00:04:29.562 --> 00:04:32.990
feel like I can learn so much from

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:35.050
and I just soak up everything I can

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:38.060
and ask as many questions,
and just gain knowledge.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.519
- So you've had a really
massive yeah, I would say.

00:04:40.519 --> 00:04:41.720
But I'm not trying to
put words in your mouth.

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:43.050
But it seems to me, massive!

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:45.764
So you're album was released
widespread, critical acclaimed.

00:04:45.764 --> 00:04:47.692
They knew, they know about you.

00:04:47.692 --> 00:04:49.073
They know about the talent,
you know what I mean?

00:04:49.073 --> 00:04:51.950
They're sleeping, but they're
a little awake, right?

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:53.783
Um, and that's not more than enough.

00:04:53.783 --> 00:04:56.030
Obviously, you're starring in Top Boy.

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:57.850
As I said, so important to the cultures.

00:04:57.850 --> 00:04:58.690
Something that a lot of us

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:00.840
have watched when we were growing up.

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:03.730
Did you have any idea that 2019

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:05.784
was gonna be as intense as it is?

00:05:05.784 --> 00:05:07.530
And do you find it overwhelming,

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:10.110
or is it like, "Yeah, this is that time?"

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:12.155
- I didn't have the greatest 2018,

00:05:12.155 --> 00:05:15.410
and I think that sparked something in me.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.345
And sometimes like, I think like sometimes

00:05:17.345 --> 00:05:20.380
negativity like breeds positivity,

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:21.910
which is cool, but I definitely

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:25.000
didn't expect it to be this wild,

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.880
but I'm grateful, I'm very grateful.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.570
- Yeah all right, so
I want to speak to you

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:30.760
about as a North Londoner, right?

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:31.978
You grew up in North London?
- Mm hm.

00:05:31.978 --> 00:05:33.180
- North London trough and through.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:34.630
I'm a South Londoner.
- Really?

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:35.463
- Yeah.

00:05:35.463 --> 00:05:36.735
So if you were trying to convince me

00:05:36.735 --> 00:05:39.538
to switch sides and convert
to the North London tribe,

00:05:39.538 --> 00:05:41.410
even though that would never happen.

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:43.318
I promise, I'm still
loyal to South London.

00:05:43.318 --> 00:05:45.190
How would you sell it to me?

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:46.150
- Do you know what?

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:51.150
It just feels like...very communal.

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:53.330
Like, everyone knows each other.

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:54.570
But the thing is that with South;

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:57.620
sought feels like, just very big.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:00.291
- Yeah, and the transport
links are like, not as great.

00:06:00.291 --> 00:06:01.140
(Gena laughs loudly)

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:02.840
- Right.
- We don't have a Tube really.

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:04.270
Yeah, yeah, okay.
- So that's the...

00:06:04.270 --> 00:06:06.580
Okay, so of course, so
I think you'd be able

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:08.470
to get around quicker in North,

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:11.490
and things like, you
can walk places, and--

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:12.323
- So it's gonna be near London--

00:06:12.323 --> 00:06:14.810
But I think, if you, you
know what I'm saying?

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:16.480
If you've grown up in South
your whole life, so...

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:18.516
- Yeah.
- I'm not moving to South.

00:06:18.516 --> 00:06:19.349
- Okay.
(Gena laughs loudly)

00:06:19.349 --> 00:06:20.765
- In no kinda way, but
just that knda way, but...

00:06:20.765 --> 00:06:22.150
You know what I'm saying?

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:23.459
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:23.459 --> 00:06:25.390
I get it.
- London as a whole

00:06:25.390 --> 00:06:26.549
is a great place!

00:06:26.549 --> 00:06:28.526
- I agree 100%

00:06:28.526 --> 00:06:30.300
Simz, thank you so much for...

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.794
Sorry actually, with
official title: Little Simz.

00:06:32.794 --> 00:06:33.627
(Little laughs)
- Nice.

00:06:33.627 --> 00:06:35.580
- Thank you so much for chatting with me.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.696
And this was your Netfiix IX.

00:06:37.696 --> 00:06:39.202
- Um hm, thank you so much.

00:06:39.202 --> 00:06:42.619
(mid-tempo techno music)

